  <div id="lessonContent">
    <h2>1. What is an Object?</h2>
    <p><b>Object = A Profile.</b> It stores all details of one thing together, with a label for each detail.</p>
    <p>Example: One student has a name, age, city, course. Without an object, you need 4 separate variables. With an object, you need only 1 variable - <code>student</code> - and it holds all 4 details inside.</p>
    <div class="note"><b>Array vs Object:</b> <b>Array</b> = List of many things - ["Ali", "Sara", "Ahmed"]. <b>Object</b> = Details of one thing - { name: "Ali", age: 20, city: "Lahore" }. Array uses [ ], Object uses { }.</div>
    <h2>2. LIVE DEMO - Student Profile</h2>
    <p>Click a student. An object will show its full profile:</p>
    <div class="demo-card">
      <div id="demoProfile" class="profile-card"><b>👤 Select a student below</b><br>Profile will show here.</div>
      <button class="btn btn-js" onclick="showStudent(0)">Show Ali 👤</button>
      <button class="btn btn-next" onclick="showStudent(1)">Show Sara 👤</button>
      <button class="btn" onclick="showStudent(2)">Show Ahmed 👤</button>
      <p style="margin-top:10px;font-size:13px;color:#64748b">Each student is one Object inside an Array.</p>
    </div>
    <h2>3. How to Create an Object?</h2>
    <div class="code-box"><code>
<span class="text">let student = {</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">name: "Ali",</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">age: 20,</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">city: "Lahore",</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">course: "JavaScript",</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">isPassed: true</span><br>
<span class="text">};</span>
    </code></div>
    <p>Object uses <b>curly brackets { }</b>. Each detail is written as <b>key: value</b>. Key = Label, Value = Data. Pairs are separated by <b>comma ,</b>.</p>
    <h2>4. How to Read Data? - Dot Notation</h2>
    <div class="code-box"><code>
<span class="text">let student = { name: "Ali", age: 20, city: "Lahore" };</span><br><br>
<span class="text">console.log(student.name); // "Ali"</span><br>
<span class="text">console.log(student.age); // 20</span><br>
<span class="text">console.log(student.city); // "Lahore"</span><br><br>
<span class="comment" style="color:#94a3b8">// Bracket Notation - Also works, useful when key has space</span><br>
<span class="text">console.log(student["name"]); // "Ali"</span><br>
<span class="text">console.log(student["city"]); // "Lahore"</span>
    </code></div>
    <p><b>Use Dot Notation</b> - <code>student.name</code> - 99% of the time. It is shorter and cleaner.</p>
    <h2>5. How to Change / Add Data?</h2>
    <div class="code-box"><code>
<span class="text">let student = { name: "Ali", age: 20 };</span><br><br>
<span class="text">student.age = 21; // Change age - 20 to 21</span><br>
<span class="text">student.city = "Karachi"; // Add new key - city</span><br>
<span class="text">student.course = "JavaScript"; // Add new key - course</span><br><br>
<span class="text">console.log(student); // { name: "Ali", age: 21, city: "Karachi", course: "JavaScript" }</span>
    </code></div>
    <h2>6. Object Method - Function Inside Object</h2>
    <p>An object can also have a function inside it. That function is called a <b>Method</b>.</p>
    <div class="code-box"><code>
<span class="text">let student = {</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">name: "Ali",</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">age: 20,</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">sayHello: function() {</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">return "Hello, My name is " + this.name;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">}</span><br>
<span class="text">};</span><br><br>
<span class="text">console.log(student.sayHello()); // "Hello, My name is Ali"</span>
    </code></div>
    <p><b>this.name</b> means - "The name of this same object". <code>this</code> always points to the object it is inside.</p>
    <h2>7. Array of Objects - Most Important in Real Work</h2>
    <p>In real websites, you never have 1 student. You have 100 students. So you make an <b>Array of Objects</b> - A list, where each item is one object.</p>
    <div class="code-box"><code>
<span class="text">let students = [</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">{ name: "Ali", age: 20, city: "Lahore" },</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">{ name: "Sara", age: 19, city: "Karachi" },</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">{ name: "Ahmed", age: 22, city: "Islamabad" }</span><br>
<span class="text">];</span><br><br>
<span class="text">console.log(students[0].name); // "Ali" - First student, his name</span><br>
<span class="text">console.log(students[1].city); // "Karachi" - Second student, her city</span><br><br>
<span class="comment" style="color:#94a3b8">// Loop - Show all students</span><br>
<span class="text">for (let i = 0; i < students.length; i++) {</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">console.log(students[i].name + " - " + students[i].city);</span><br>
<span class="text">}</span>
    </code></div>
    <h2>8. Complete Example - Product Card</h2>
    <div class="code-box"><code>
<span class="tag">&lt;!DOCTYPE html&gt;</span><br>
<span class="tag">&lt;html&gt;</span><br>
<span class="tag">&lt;body&gt;</span><br><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="tag">&lt;h1</span> <span class="attr">id</span>=<span class="val">"product"</span><span class="tag">&gt;</span><span class="text">Product</span><span class="tag">&lt;/h1&gt;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="tag">&lt;button</span> <span class="attr">onclick</span>=<span class="val">"showProduct()"</span><span class="tag">&gt;</span><span class="text">Show Product</span><span class="tag">&lt;/button&gt;</span><br><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="tag">&lt;script&gt;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">let product = {</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">name: "Laptop",</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">price: 150000,</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">brand: "HP",</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">inStock: true</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">};</span><br><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">function showProduct() {</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">let msg = product.name + " - " + product.brand + " - Rs " + product.price;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">if (product.inStock) { msg = msg + " - In Stock"; }</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">document.getElementById("product").innerHTML = msg;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">}</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="tag">&lt;/script&gt;</span><br>
<span class="tag">&lt;/body&gt;</span><br>
<span class="tag">&lt;/html&gt;</span>
    </code></div>
    <h2>9. Homework</h2>
    <p>In Playground, build this:</p>
    <p>1. Object <code>let myProfile = { name: "Your Name", age: Your Age, city: "Your City", skill: "HTML" }</code> - Show it on page with dot notation<br>2. Array of 3 products - Each product is an object { name, price } - Use loop to show all products<br>3. Add a method <code>introduce()</code> to your profile object that returns "Hello, I am ___ and I live in ___"</p>
    <div class="box"><b>Remember:</b> Object = Profile in { } | key: value = Label: Data | Dot Notation = student.name | Bracket = student["name"] | Method = Function inside object | this = This same object | Array of Objects = List of profiles - Most used in real websites</div>
    <p><b>Next Step:</b> <a href="/lesson29">Lesson 29 - String Methods</a> - Learn how to clean, cut, and change text. Uppercase, lowercase, length, slice.</p>
